        {
          "id": 877259656,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This adds a requirement for the \"packaging\" library:\n\n```\n 1/38 Test  #1: suite_capture ..........................***Failed    0.27 sec\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\test\\test.py\", line 25, in <module>\n    import fixtures_ws\n  File \"C:\\builds\\wireshark\\wireshark\\test\\fixtures_ws.py\", line 11, in <module>\n    from packaging import version\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'packaging'\n```\n\nWould it make sense to convert the version to an [integer tuple](https://stackoverflow.com/a/11887821/82195) instead? As noted elsewhere in the StackOverflow discussion this isn't a good general solution, but in our case we know that we're comparing pairs of ints.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789887783",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-03-16T15:48:14.184Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-03-16T16:07:25.175Z",
